 {grade:3,text:'Eli noticed that his paper airplane always turned left. He checked the wings and saw that one was bent higher than the other. He made them even and tested it again. The airplane flew straight across the room.',character:'Eli',setting:'A room',first:'The airplane turned left.',detail:'One wing was bent higher.',main:'Eli improves his airplane by testing it.',cause:'The wings were uneven',inference:'Eli uses observations to solve a problem.',fact:'The airplane flew straight after the change.'},
 {grade:3,text:'Sea turtles lay eggs in nests on sandy beaches. After hatching, young turtles move toward the sea. Bright lights near beaches can confuse them. Keeping nesting beaches dark can help young turtles find the water.',character:'Sea turtles',setting:'Sandy beaches',first:'Sea turtles lay eggs in nests.',detail:'Bright lights',main:'Dark beaches help young sea turtles.',cause:'Bright lights can confuse young turtles',inference:'People can help protect sea turtles.',fact:'Young turtles move toward the sea.'},
 {grade:3,text:'Nia and her neighbors collected litter at the park. They wore gloves and sorted safe recyclable items into a separate bag. By noon, the walking path was clear. Nia suggested placing a sign beside the bins to help visitors sort their trash.',character:'Nia',setting:'The park',first:'They collected litter.',detail:'Gloves',main:'Neighbors work together to care for a park.',cause:'To help visitors sort their trash',inference:'Nia wants the park to stay clean.',fact:'The walking path was clear by noon.'},
 {grade:3,text:'A cactus stores water in its thick stem. Its waxy surface helps reduce water loss. Many cacti have spines instead of broad leaves. These features help cacti live where rain is scarce.',character:'A cactus',setting:'A place where rain is scarce',first:'A cactus stores water in its stem.',detail:'A thick stem',main:'Cactus features help it conserve water.',cause:'To reduce water loss',inference:'A cactus is suited to dry places.',fact:'Many cacti have spines.'},
 {grade:3,text:'Mateo promised to bring markers for the class poster. In the morning, he could not find them. He checked his art drawer, packed the markers, and arrived before the group began. His friends thanked him, and they planned their design together.',character:'Mateo',setting:'A classroom',first:'Mateo promised to bring markers.',detail:'Markers',main:'Mateo keeps his promise to his group.',cause:'They needed markers for the poster',inference:'Mateo is dependable.',fact:'They planned the design together.'}
